Update an existing link, specified by its link ID. Only its name and tags can be updated.

USAGE:
  scw interlink link update <link-id ...> [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  link-id           ID of the link to update
  [name]            Name of the link
  [tags.{index}]    List of tags to apply to the link
  [peer-asn]        For self-hosted links, AS Number to establish BGP session.
  [region=fr-par]   Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par | it-mil | nl-ams | pl-waw)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for update
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
